    "description": "ENTEK Technology Holdings manufactures battery separators and related components used in lithium-ion battery applications. Its customers are battery manufacturers and other participants in the electric-vehicle and energy-storage supply chain that require separator materials and domestic manufacturing capacity. The business follows an asset-heavy industrial model based on specialized manufacturing plants, process technology, and long-term customer qualification cycles. Public materials describe ENTEK as operating in Oregon and expanding manufacturing capacity in Indiana as part of a broader effort to reshore critical U.S. battery supply-chain infrastructure. I Squared announced an agreement to acquire a majority equity interest in September 2025 and committed up to $800 million to support expansion; the exact current ownership percentage is not publicly disclosed in the company announcement. The investment aligns with I Squared’s energy-transition strategy around industrial infrastructure needed for electrification.",
